        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2cb4adfe-c1c3-53c5-846a-1300c6cc5959",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeremy Brock, Kevin Macdonald, Channing Tatum, Jamie Bell, Donald Sutherland, Rosemary Sutcliff, Alexandros Avranas\n- Works: Mrs Brown, Driving Lessons, The Last King of Scotland, Charlotte Gray, The Eagle, The Eagle of the Ninth, True Crimes\n- Roles: writer, director, screenwriter\n- Topics: film adaptation, historical drama, crime drama-thriller\n\nFacts:\n- Rosemary Sutcliff wrote the historical adventure novel \"The Eagle of the Ninth\" in 1954.\n- Jeremy Brock, born in 1959, is an English writer and director.\n- Jeremy Brock's works include the screenplays \"Mrs Brown,\" \"Driving Lessons,\" \"The Last King of Scotland,\" \"Charlotte Gray,\" and \"The Eagle.\"\n- \"The Eagle\" is a 2011 epic historical drama film set in Roman Britain.\n- Kevin Macdonald directed \"The Eagle.\"\n- Channing Tatum, Jamie Bell, and Donald Sutherland starred in \"The Eagle.\"\n- Jeremy Brock adapted \"The Eagle\" from Rosemary Sutcliff's novel \"The Eagle of the Ninth.\"\n- \"The Eagle\" follows a young Roman officer searching northern Great Britain for the lost eagle standard of his father's legion.\n- \"True Crimes\" is a 2016 American-Polish crime drama-thriller film.\n- Alexandros Avranas directed \"True Crimes.\"\n- Jeremy Brock wrote \"True Crimes.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
